    {
      "id": 99,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        0,
        620
      ],
      "size": [
        340,
        420
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 98,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "title": "READ ME",
      "widgets_values": [
        "StereoForge - single image -> side-by-side stereo\n\n1. Load any image. Downscaling is OFF by default: the input is copied bit-exactly into its eye.\n2. StereoSpace (depth-free stereo diffusion) renders the opposite eye at ~0.6 MP; auto_comfort runs a short probe, measures real binocular parallax and re-renders with a baseline that gives the nearest content ~2.5% of width parallax.\n3. Lift: RAFT correspondence between the pair -> edge-snapped full-res disparity -> z-buffered resampling of the ORIGINAL pixels. Disocclusions, out-of-frame strips and regions where the generator disagrees (reflections, glass, speculars) come from the generated view.\n4. Tiled Masked Refine re-details only those regions at native resolution (FLUX.1-dev, denoise 0.5).\n   To skip it, bypass the refine node (Ctrl+B) - output stays valid, just softer in filled areas.\n5. Compose: parallel (L|R) or cross-eyed. Output is exactly 2W x H.\n\ngenerate_eye=left keeps the input as the RIGHT eye (output is still L|R ordered)."
      ]
    }
